WEBVTT

00:27.470 --> 00:29.470
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

01:42.790 --> 01:45.500
EPISODE 51: PEACEFUL DAYS
Good work, Great Rimuru!

01:45.500 --> 01:48.250
EPISODE 51: PEACEFUL DAYS
Aww, stop it.

01:48.250 --> 01:49.170
Hm?

01:49.590 --> 01:51.060
Where is Hakuro?

01:51.670 --> 01:54.910
He still had stuff to take care of,
so he went back.

01:57.310 --> 02:00.180
I see. So they have Hakuro
to clean up the rest for them.

02:00.680 --> 02:03.780
He's currently working with Geld
to investigate Clayman's castle,

02:03.780 --> 02:07.230
divide the war spoils,
and handle the prisoners.

02:07.230 --> 02:08.190
I see.

02:08.570 --> 02:09.790
Wait, Benimaru.

02:09.790 --> 02:12.690
You're the commander.
Is it okay for you to be here?

02:13.860 --> 02:18.450
With the war over, there is no reason
for us to stay there forever.

02:19.160 --> 02:24.040
So I gave my command over to my talented
vice-commander and left the scene.

02:24.460 --> 02:28.170
So he had the Three Beastketeers
to take care of the rest.

02:28.630 --> 02:31.670
That's siblings for you.
They both think alike.

02:32.060 --> 02:34.800
I wish they would learn about
taking responsibility from me—

02:34.800 --> 02:38.140
Answer. It is presumed to be the result
of them learning from their master.

02:38.550 --> 02:41.770
Don't "presume" that!
You know that has to be wrong!

02:41.770 --> 02:44.230
You sure your computing
capability didn't decline

02:44.230 --> 02:46.650
when you evolved from
the Great Sage to Raphael?

02:46.650 --> 02:47.560
Negative.

02:47.560 --> 02:49.980
Such a phenomenon
has not been detected.

02:49.980 --> 02:51.820
She denied it...

02:54.670 --> 02:58.320
So, I heard Gabiru go back
to the battlefield.

02:58.320 --> 02:59.140
Yes.

02:59.140 --> 03:03.040
He formed a friendship with
a follower of Lady Milim named Middray

03:03.040 --> 03:05.710
and is currently helping him
clean up after the battle.

03:07.880 --> 03:09.250
I see.

03:09.250 --> 03:11.590
War is a lot of work
even after you win them.

03:12.380 --> 03:15.050
Transporting all the POWs
from the site is a lot of work,

03:15.050 --> 03:18.590
it would be troublesome if they revolted
when our eyes weren't on them.

03:18.590 --> 03:19.850
Rest assured.

03:20.180 --> 03:23.020
I brought them all together
and gave some explanations.

03:23.020 --> 03:25.690
Just what kind of "explanation" he gave?

03:26.220 --> 03:27.940
Then what about Gabiru?

03:27.940 --> 03:30.900
I believe he will return soon,
along with the Three Beastketeers.

03:30.900 --> 03:33.320
What? They'll be coming too?

03:33.320 --> 03:37.780
Lady Milim blew away
the capital of Eurazania, didn't she?

03:38.950 --> 03:44.540
So, we agreed to house them
in our nation for the time being.

03:44.540 --> 03:46.210
But we can't take all of them, can we?

03:46.710 --> 03:49.460
We decided to split them up.

03:50.000 --> 03:52.880
We have those who still have
their village to return there.

03:52.880 --> 03:57.470
Those who come to Tempest will be
the ones who wish to learn new skills.

03:58.090 --> 04:01.850
Lycanthrope and Majin with muscle
would join Geld's command

04:01.850 --> 04:04.350
to redevelop Eurazania's vacant land.

04:04.350 --> 04:05.980
Oh, now that he mentions it...

04:06.850 --> 04:10.510
Eurazania became
a part of Milim's territory.

04:10.980 --> 04:16.740
I suggested she move her capital there
since they were building it from scratch.

04:16.740 --> 04:18.910
A new capital?

04:18.910 --> 04:20.570
I'll make it, then!

04:21.990 --> 04:25.240
But those who will come here
won't be just the Lycanthropes,

04:25.240 --> 04:27.120
but also Majin prisoners.

04:27.120 --> 04:30.630
Just in case, I'll tell them
to keep their guard up.

04:30.630 --> 04:32.310
Right.

04:32.310 --> 04:34.750
I'll "explain" stuff to everyone.

04:36.010 --> 04:37.230
I'm counting on you.

04:37.830 --> 04:42.010
They all make their own decision
without needing me to order them.

04:42.010 --> 04:44.510
What a reliable bunch.

04:44.510 --> 04:46.020
Wait, hold up...

04:46.020 --> 04:50.020
Could it be they
don't need me anymore?

04:50.520 --> 04:53.730
- That makes me lonely a little.
- I'll be in charge of security, then.

04:53.730 --> 04:55.020
Leave it to me!

04:56.610 --> 05:00.280
Great Rimuru, the negotiations
proceeded according to plan.

05:01.330 --> 05:04.660
This is the proof of our peace treaty...

05:05.080 --> 05:09.210
...and fifteen hundred stellars
as part of the reparation.

05:10.160 --> 05:12.460
That's a lot more than we expected.

05:12.460 --> 05:14.590
I suppose Falmuth is a big kingdom.

05:14.590 --> 05:16.230
Yes.

05:16.230 --> 05:20.970
However, the majority of this was
from King Edmaris's personal fund.

05:21.380 --> 05:24.640
The royalists knew that without
the knight to protect them,

05:24.640 --> 05:29.480
the nobles would be taking
everything from them either way.

05:29.480 --> 05:30.890
I see.

05:30.890 --> 05:33.850
So do you think there
will be a civil war soon?

05:33.850 --> 05:35.860
Yes, without a doubt.

05:36.610 --> 05:40.520
The remaining balance exists
in the form of an outstanding loan,

05:40.520 --> 05:43.240
but I doubt the new king will abide
by that agreement for long.

05:43.240 --> 05:49.660
With that in mind, instead of the prince,
I had the king's brother take the throne.

05:49.660 --> 05:51.080
Report.

05:51.080 --> 05:54.580
The faction that refuses to pay
the rest of the reparations

05:54.580 --> 05:58.000
will likely try to push all
the responsibility on Edmaris.

05:58.000 --> 05:59.200
Right.

06:00.170 --> 06:02.930
After leaving the throne
and becoming a viscount,

06:02.930 --> 06:06.230
Edmaris would be shortly moving to
a small rural land in the countryside,

06:06.230 --> 06:08.210
near Count Earl Nidol Migam's
own lands.

06:08.210 --> 06:11.600
Nidol's domain is home to Youm's band,

06:11.600 --> 06:14.770
so they can come help out
if anything happens.

06:14.770 --> 06:16.940
Yes, precisely.

06:16.940 --> 06:20.070
Even if the new king
tried to cut off Edmaris,

06:20.070 --> 06:22.070
Youm would be there to stop it.

06:22.070 --> 06:27.700
And denouncing the new king for
his insincerity would lead to a civil war.

06:28.490 --> 06:34.580
He made it so conflict would emerge naturally
by having Youm protect Edmaris.

06:34.580 --> 06:35.910
That's a perfect plan.

06:36.810 --> 06:38.460
Don't let your guard down, all right?

06:38.460 --> 06:40.960
I want you to keep civilian
casualties to a minimum.

06:41.630 --> 06:43.220
As you wish, my lord.

06:43.220 --> 06:44.430
I'm counting on you.

06:44.430 --> 06:48.220
If you need more funds,
go ahead and use these stellars.

06:48.220 --> 06:53.340
I'm truly delighted by your consideration,
but that will not be necessary.

06:53.340 --> 06:55.690
If possible, I'd like the permission
to fight myself—

06:55.690 --> 06:57.940
Uh, anything but that.

06:57.940 --> 07:01.730
I'll give you troops to work with,
so try to lay yourself low, okay?

07:02.360 --> 07:03.610
Very well.

07:03.940 --> 07:06.900
I will remain firmly behind the scenes.

07:07.470 --> 07:09.860
You should learn a thing or two
from Diablo, Shion.

07:09.860 --> 07:14.660
What?! But I have never failed
to follow your orders, Great Rimuru!

07:15.620 --> 07:20.670
That reminds me. Western Holy Church
tried to make contact with Reyhiem.

07:20.670 --> 07:22.170
Reyhiem?

07:22.670 --> 07:25.840
Oh, that archbishop guy.

07:26.320 --> 07:30.470
The Church appears to be seeking
to learn more about the war with Falmuth,

07:30.470 --> 07:33.470
so they summoned him
to hear his explanation.

07:33.470 --> 07:35.270
What should we do about that?

07:36.980 --> 07:39.980
t sounds like it'll be troublesome
if we ignore them.

07:39.980 --> 07:41.150
It would.

07:41.150 --> 07:43.360
I think it best to allow him
to testify to them

07:43.360 --> 07:45.990
to see what their next move will be.

07:46.700 --> 07:47.990
Right.

07:48.700 --> 07:54.010
There were just three survivors,
so of course they would want more info.

07:54.860 --> 07:58.370
But I heard the Church
is monitoring Veldora,

07:58.370 --> 08:00.880
so they likely could tell
if we try to lie to them.

08:00.880 --> 08:03.960
Shall I have him speak the truth, then?

08:06.550 --> 08:08.550
Let's record a message into this.

08:08.970 --> 08:13.060
We can have Reyhiem take it over there
and see how the Church reacts.

08:13.060 --> 08:14.310
Very well.

08:15.220 --> 08:16.480
Great Rimuru!

08:16.480 --> 08:17.440
What?

08:17.730 --> 08:20.940
The refugees and the POWs have arrived!

08:27.260 --> 08:29.320
They got here earlier than expected.

08:29.320 --> 08:30.700
Lord Rimuru.

08:30.700 --> 08:32.450
Albis, Suphia!

08:32.830 --> 08:36.450
Thank you very much for
accepting our brethren.

08:36.450 --> 08:38.290
No biggie.

08:38.290 --> 08:40.580
Oh, is Phobio not with you two?

08:40.580 --> 08:44.170
Phobio stayed behind to watch
over the remaining prisoners.

08:44.170 --> 08:48.340
We had him keep a glaring eye on the prisoners
to ensure no revolts took place.

08:48.670 --> 08:52.090
In other words, they were pushing
the boring work on him.

08:52.090 --> 08:54.680
Sorry about that, Phobio.

08:54.680 --> 08:56.970
We're all ready over here.

08:56.970 --> 08:59.980
The temporary housing
inspection is over

08:59.980 --> 09:03.230
and we already have an idea of
how to assign jobs to everyone.

09:03.980 --> 09:06.070
I'll fill you in the details later.

09:06.070 --> 09:08.650
- Okay.
- We'll excuse ourselves now.

09:11.660 --> 09:13.410
Great Rimuru!

09:14.160 --> 09:15.700
I have returned.

09:15.700 --> 09:17.290
Oh, welcome back.

09:17.870 --> 09:19.870
I heard you did well in battle.

09:19.870 --> 09:22.920
No, no! I still have so much to learn!

09:23.250 --> 09:26.420
Sir Middray beat me to a pulp.

09:26.420 --> 09:28.420
Oh, that. Benimaru told me about it.

09:29.010 --> 09:31.930
He's an absurdly strong Dragonewt, right?

09:32.430 --> 09:37.680
Well, they all worship Milim,
so I bet he really loves fighting.

09:37.680 --> 09:41.020
You aren't exactly weak yourself.
You still have much more room to grow.

09:41.020 --> 09:46.190
I, Gabiru, am prepared to do my best
to live up to your lofty expectations!

09:46.690 --> 09:47.900
By the way...

09:47.900 --> 09:48.940
What's this?

09:49.260 --> 09:52.360
Lady Milim told me to give it to you.

09:52.360 --> 09:53.970
From Milim?

09:55.450 --> 09:56.910
This is Milim!

09:56.910 --> 10:01.620
Next time I visit, I'll be bringing along
some guys who love to care for me!

10:01.620 --> 10:06.090
I want you to teach them everything
there is to know about cooking.

10:06.090 --> 10:08.000
This is an earnest request!

10:08.000 --> 10:10.590
We are buddies,
so I really need your help!

10:10.590 --> 10:13.590
Please, please, please!

10:14.390 --> 10:17.260
Did she tell you what this is about?

10:17.260 --> 10:20.140
Yes, a little bit.

10:20.140 --> 10:24.060
I met a member of the Dragon Faithful
named Sir Hermes while I was there.

10:24.060 --> 10:28.770
He's a free-spirited man who's traveled to
the Dwarven Kingdom and Western Nations.

10:28.770 --> 10:31.030
He told me about a lot of stuff.

10:31.030 --> 10:33.110
And as he puts it,

10:33.450 --> 10:36.780
the Dragon Faithful
lives a life of frugality.

10:36.780 --> 10:40.740
And the food they present to Lady Milim
isn't cooked in any way whatsoever.

10:40.740 --> 10:42.120
I see.

10:42.450 --> 10:48.130
Perhaps they share some tastes with us,
enjoying a fish best when it's raw.

10:48.460 --> 10:50.880
I don't think that's quite right.

10:50.880 --> 10:52.170
What do you mean?

10:52.170 --> 10:55.180
Dragonewts got the same sense
of taste as humans, right?

10:55.180 --> 10:57.430
Yes, we do! Thanks to
my glorious evolution,

10:57.430 --> 10:59.510
I have gained a wondrous
set of taste buds!

10:59.890 --> 11:04.640
All meals were bland to me, but it is now
one of the best delights I can wish for!

11:04.640 --> 11:05.810
Right?

11:05.810 --> 11:08.250
So when you eat a good meal,

11:08.250 --> 11:11.440
don't you feel like you
want to taste it again?

11:11.440 --> 11:16.410
I see! So that's what Sir Hermes
was trying to say!

11:16.410 --> 11:21.160
But then, why can't Milim just
say that directly to her people?

11:21.160 --> 11:24.600
Well, in her own unique way,
she knows how to read the room.

11:25.080 --> 11:28.920
In that case, let's give them
all the royal treatment they deserve!

11:28.920 --> 11:31.800
Yes, sir! A splendid idea!

11:31.800 --> 11:33.570
I shall be off now, then!

11:52.230 --> 11:55.240
The town seems to be full of life.

11:55.240 --> 11:57.150
A month had passed
since Walpurgis Council.

11:57.150 --> 12:01.240
Seems like our new residents finally
gotten used to their life here.

12:01.240 --> 12:03.540
Oh, Great Rimuru.

12:03.540 --> 12:05.200
Over there.

12:08.620 --> 12:10.380
Geld?

12:10.380 --> 12:11.540
Great Rimuru...

12:11.860 --> 12:13.630
He looks tired.

12:13.630 --> 12:15.070
So it seems.

12:17.970 --> 12:21.050
So what happened?

12:22.180 --> 12:27.270
I, Geld, have a newfound
respect for you, Great Rimuru.

12:27.270 --> 12:28.730
Where did that come from?

12:29.350 --> 12:31.310
Well, actually...

12:32.130 --> 12:35.230
I was organizing the prisoners,
putting them in groups,

12:35.230 --> 12:38.320
and do some surveying
and land-clearing work...

12:38.320 --> 12:41.870
But several problems surfaced.

12:43.080 --> 12:45.530
High Orcs had no problem

12:45.530 --> 12:48.120
using Thought Communication
to chat with one another,

12:48.120 --> 12:51.290
but we can't do that with
the Lycanthropes or Majins.

12:52.580 --> 12:57.210
There were also several Majins
who weren't fond of being ordered around,

12:57.530 --> 13:01.010
and even those who do have the drive
to work can't yield much result.

13:01.010 --> 13:02.850
I see.

13:02.850 --> 13:06.720
To use people and educate them
is a difficult task.

13:08.750 --> 13:11.480
Your story reminds me of
when I was still an office worker.

13:11.480 --> 13:14.060
This calls for a drink!

13:14.480 --> 13:16.820
Let's have a drink tonight, Geld!

13:16.820 --> 13:20.320
Yes! Thank you very much,
Great Rimuru!

13:22.820 --> 13:24.360
Sounds like you had it tough.

13:25.230 --> 13:28.500
More people didn't
always mean better work.

13:28.500 --> 13:34.290
But it is also impossible to make them
grow all at the same pace.

13:34.290 --> 13:37.500
It makes you think it'd be faster
to just do the job yourselves,

13:37.500 --> 13:40.340
but then those under you
won't get any experience.

13:41.220 --> 13:44.300
At this rate, I can't be useful
for Great Rimuru...

13:45.760 --> 13:48.520
There, there. Don't mind it.

13:48.930 --> 13:50.770
This really takes me back.

13:51.280 --> 13:53.770
Field workers who won't listen to orders.

13:53.770 --> 13:56.770
Junior who tries to hide their mistakes.

13:56.770 --> 14:00.610
And boss who would push
the blame on others.

14:01.200 --> 14:05.910
I have a lot of good memories, too,
but there's also no end to the bad ones.

14:05.910 --> 14:08.620
Another one helping, please!
A strong one!

14:08.620 --> 14:09.620
Coming right up.

14:10.780 --> 14:13.170
So that's why you went out
drinking with Geld all night?

14:13.170 --> 14:17.290
But I can't get drunk at all
because of Poison Nullification.

14:17.290 --> 14:20.630
Well, not getting a hangover
is a nice thing, though.

14:20.630 --> 14:21.800
Great Rimuru!

14:22.800 --> 14:24.180
Oh, what's the matter?

14:24.180 --> 14:26.550
The merchants had begun
returning to town.

14:26.910 --> 14:30.020
Thanks to Sir Fuze declaring
things are safe now,

14:30.430 --> 14:33.390
we're getting more people
coming in and going.

14:33.390 --> 14:35.520
I see. That's great news.

14:35.910 --> 14:40.860
There are no big moves from other nations
following your crowning as a Demon Lord.

14:40.860 --> 14:43.490
Well, I'm sure they're wary of us.

14:43.490 --> 14:44.280
Yes.

14:44.780 --> 14:49.240
The emperor of the Sorcerous Dynasty
of Thalion, Elmesia El-Ru Thalion

14:49.240 --> 14:52.830
has declared their formal
relations with Tempest.

14:52.830 --> 14:55.870
So she's saying, "Hurry and build
the highway already," huh?

14:55.870 --> 14:59.800
Her statement had led to much
consternation among all the world leaders

14:59.800 --> 15:01.840
according to Sir Fuze.

15:02.790 --> 15:05.430
All our relations are
fulfilling their sworn duty

15:05.430 --> 15:08.970
and working hard on our
behalf across the world!

15:08.970 --> 15:09.930
I see.

15:11.430 --> 15:14.770
If I remember, the one in charge of
the prior survey for the highway was...

15:15.940 --> 15:22.530
I did not find any hostile monsters
present around the projected route.

15:22.530 --> 15:27.740
When I explained your plans to them,
they all readily agreed to it.

15:27.740 --> 15:29.320
That's great.

15:29.670 --> 15:32.160
In that case, make sure
to wrap up the survey

15:32.160 --> 15:34.710
and other work by the time
Geld's free again.

15:34.710 --> 15:37.460
But there is one issue.

15:37.460 --> 15:38.580
Oh, what is it?

15:38.990 --> 15:42.250
The Forest of Jura
is in your jurisdiction,

15:42.250 --> 15:45.090
but the Kusha Mountains
lie on one of its borders.

15:45.840 --> 15:48.430
The area is filled with high peaks
and treacherous canyons,

15:48.430 --> 15:52.260
and the peaks are said to be
populated by the Tengu.

15:53.280 --> 15:55.480
This information was
from the local populace,

15:55.480 --> 15:57.600
so it's difficult to dismiss.

15:57.600 --> 16:00.110
What do you mean by that?

16:00.980 --> 16:06.110
The Tengu are said to be friendly,
but they are a warrior race at their core.

16:06.110 --> 16:11.200
Even that Lady Frey avoided
direct conflict with them.

16:11.200 --> 16:13.430
I would suggest seeking
her advice about this.

16:13.870 --> 16:15.700
- Then I'll—
- One moment.

16:16.250 --> 16:17.750
I'll go.

16:17.750 --> 16:22.290
A Demon Lord coming to them
without notice could make them wary.

16:22.290 --> 16:23.710
I see.

16:23.710 --> 16:25.170
Then, I'll leave it to you.

16:25.170 --> 16:29.680
You've seemed rather friendly
with Lady Albis as of late.

16:29.680 --> 16:32.430
You're not volunteering to have
a tryst with her, aren't you?

16:32.430 --> 16:35.020
Huh?! Benimaru and Albis?

16:35.020 --> 16:37.100
Care to explain yourself, Benimaru?

16:37.100 --> 16:38.980
You misunderstand her, Great Rimuru.

16:38.980 --> 16:41.650
Shuna, enough of your nonsense.

16:42.480 --> 16:44.150
Don't worry, Great Rimuru.

16:44.150 --> 16:47.690
Whether Benimaru is here or not,
you will always have me!

16:48.610 --> 16:50.410
What are you talking about?

16:51.160 --> 16:54.830
You fell for Albis's honey trap and planned
to abandon our nation, didn't you?

16:54.830 --> 16:58.620
Shion, how on earth
are you interpreting things that way?

16:58.620 --> 17:00.670
Yeah, I really doubt that.

17:01.500 --> 17:03.590
You heard him, Shion.

17:03.590 --> 17:06.880
Great Rimuru,
you do trust in me, yes?

17:06.880 --> 17:12.140
You're my trusted right-hand man.
It's not a matter of trust by now.

17:12.140 --> 17:17.470
Anyway, if we keep talking about this,
Shion might get wild ideas.

17:17.470 --> 17:19.350
Benimaru, I'm assigning this job to you!

17:19.350 --> 17:20.390
Yes, sir.

17:27.150 --> 17:30.820
There are a lot of problems
here and there.

17:32.610 --> 17:36.160
I suppose I'll call everyone today
for a meeting.

17:37.700 --> 17:39.910
Sorry for calling you
all of a sudden.

17:40.330 --> 17:43.830
No, not a problem.

17:43.830 --> 17:47.420
I have to say, though,
Geld has it far worse.

17:47.420 --> 17:51.010
I finished transferring
leadership over last night,

17:51.010 --> 17:53.800
so there's no need for me
to go back over there.

17:53.800 --> 17:56.560
Yeah, sounds like it troubles him a lot.

17:56.560 --> 18:00.020
He would have it easier if he was
willing to compromise on matters,

18:00.020 --> 18:02.440
but he was always far
too serious-minded for that.

18:04.690 --> 18:08.610
Also, I have something else
to report to you.

18:08.610 --> 18:09.820
What's that?

18:09.820 --> 18:13.860
About Clayman's land of
the Puppet Nation Distave.

18:13.860 --> 18:16.280
The only ones living there
were dark elves tasked

18:16.280 --> 18:18.740
with maintaining and managing
the castle grounds.

18:18.740 --> 18:21.660
They all showed the will to obey us.

18:21.660 --> 18:23.170
Right. So?

18:24.990 --> 18:26.650
As they described it to me,

18:26.650 --> 18:31.170
Distave used to be home
to a kingdom of elves,

18:31.170 --> 18:34.630
and remarkably enough,
there were ruins remaining in the land.

18:34.630 --> 18:38.140
They described themselves
as the grave keepers.

18:38.140 --> 18:43.100
Huh? So you're saying there are ruins
from an ancient kingdom in there?

18:43.100 --> 18:44.600
I see.

18:44.600 --> 18:49.230
Perhaps Clayman derived much of his riches
from the things discovered there.

18:49.230 --> 18:51.940
Ancient ruins were
dotted all over the world

18:51.940 --> 18:55.860
and often raided by those who made
treasure hunting their line of work.

18:56.320 --> 19:01.790
However, only a precious few ruins
have been discovered so far.

19:02.500 --> 19:05.670
Hakuro, I want you to keep
this discovery a secret.

19:05.670 --> 19:08.750
I want to decide after I go there
and see things for myself.

19:08.750 --> 19:09.800
Yes, sir.

19:12.300 --> 19:14.140
Um, everyone...

19:14.140 --> 19:17.010
As some of you already know,

19:17.010 --> 19:20.140
I have been promoted to Demon Lord!

19:20.140 --> 19:22.520
Congratulation!

19:24.600 --> 19:26.190
We have finally made it!

19:26.190 --> 19:28.860
It's really amazing!
I'm filled with joy!

19:29.270 --> 19:31.690
It is the start of a new era
for Great Rimuru!

19:31.690 --> 19:33.860
Ah, right. I didn't mention this,

19:33.860 --> 19:37.950
but it's been decided that
I now rule the entire Jura forest!

19:38.990 --> 19:43.090
I'm already calling myself the Chancellor,
so there shouldn't be an issue, right?

19:44.000 --> 19:47.540
What? Did I say something bad?

19:47.540 --> 19:49.290
Um...

19:49.290 --> 19:52.000
The whole forest? Truly?

19:52.000 --> 19:53.550
Y-Yeah...

19:53.550 --> 19:55.670
Are you serious?

19:55.670 --> 19:59.300
That means including everything
on the other side of the river, right?

19:59.300 --> 20:00.260
I think so.

20:00.550 --> 20:02.930
Is there a problem?

20:02.930 --> 20:05.980
Not exactly a "problem,"

20:05.980 --> 20:10.270
but I don't believe the area past
the river counts as the Dryads' domain.

20:10.810 --> 20:13.440
You are recognized as
a Chancellor only of the lands

20:13.440 --> 20:16.410
that the Dryads themselves have built up.

20:16.900 --> 20:19.030
To the denizens beyond the river,

20:19.030 --> 20:22.780
the advent of a new Demon Lord would
likely prove to be quite a headache.

20:24.450 --> 20:27.410
If you asked me,
this is an astounding development.

20:27.410 --> 20:31.250
This means the Demon
Lords have formally agreed

20:31.250 --> 20:35.960
that you have rights to all
the forest's natural resources.

20:35.960 --> 20:41.390
People had been harvesting the forest's
resources tacitly for a while now.

20:41.390 --> 20:47.480
But now, anyone who wishes to dwell
in the forest must obtain your permission.

20:47.480 --> 20:50.850
And there are a lot of people
already living in the forest right now.

20:50.850 --> 20:56.190
That means people will be coming
here to ask for my permission?

20:56.190 --> 20:57.820
I'm sure they would.

20:57.820 --> 21:00.660
Now that you're officially a Demon Lord,

21:00.660 --> 21:03.620
anyone who fails to greet you
could be legally branded a rebel.

21:04.120 --> 21:05.870
Why worry about that now?

21:05.870 --> 21:11.120
It's important! A Demon Lord
is a proud symbol of power!

21:11.120 --> 21:16.760
Even the lizardmen were desperate
to get the protection of a Demon Lord!

21:16.760 --> 21:22.300
Defying one was unthinkable,
and ignoring one is the height of folly!

21:22.740 --> 21:25.600
It's not like I care much about that,
though.

21:25.970 --> 21:29.680
At the very least, the lizardmen
will be coming to see you soon.

21:29.680 --> 21:33.900
I already told my father
of your ascension!

21:34.320 --> 21:35.820
You mean Abiru? He's coming?

21:35.820 --> 21:36.820
He is!

21:36.820 --> 21:38.860
He told Lady Shion about it as well,

21:38.860 --> 21:43.490
but he wishes to see you in all
your demonic glory for himself!

21:44.330 --> 21:46.510
I'm sure Great Rimuru
would expect nothing less!

21:46.510 --> 21:48.790
Wait, you didn't tell me
anything about this, Shion!

21:49.580 --> 21:57.300
But if the lizardmen are coming to see me,
that means smaller tribes are as well.

21:58.130 --> 21:59.970
Which means...

21:59.970 --> 22:02.680
Oh! If that is the case...

22:03.800 --> 22:05.550
I just had an idea.

22:05.550 --> 22:11.310
Why don't we turn this into a big campaign
and use it to unveil this town?

22:11.700 --> 22:13.600
Rather than going one at a time,

22:13.600 --> 22:15.920
it'd be easier to have them all
come in one go, no?

22:16.440 --> 22:18.320
What do you mean?

22:18.320 --> 22:22.150
We still have space for more people
to come and live here.

22:22.150 --> 22:24.870
In fact, we're in need
of more workforce.

22:25.720 --> 22:29.950
We'll show the town to everyone
and aim to expand our population.

22:29.950 --> 22:34.290
If they'll be coming to see me anyway,
let's have them learn about this town too.

22:34.290 --> 22:38.220
Once they have, maybe some of them
would think of migrating here.

22:38.670 --> 22:41.840
We'll need to welcome Milim, too.

22:42.350 --> 22:46.300
Plus, we've all been on
pins and needles as of late,

22:46.300 --> 22:48.760
so why don't we kick back a little bit?

22:48.760 --> 22:52.350
So I'm saying let's hold
a big festival together!

22:52.680 --> 22:53.850
A festival!

22:54.230 --> 22:56.350
Let's do it!
It will be a magnificent event!

22:56.860 --> 22:59.650
If I'll have to make
my public debut anyway,

22:59.650 --> 23:03.240
let's make it
the biggest one we can!

23:03.240 --> 23:04.610
Yes, sir!

24:36.540 --> 24:39.580
Next time, "Each Respective Roles."
